## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests dynamic programming on partitioning with a non-linear cost function (distinct character count). It's concrete, implementable, and scales well to typical interview constraints.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes and partition count
- Precomputing distinct character counts for all substrings (O(n²) with two pointers)
- Reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time/space trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPartitionDistinct(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const dist = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(n).fill(0));

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    const seen = new Set();
    for (let j = i; j < n; j++) {
      seen.add(s[j]);
      dist[i][j] = seen.size;
    }
  }

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prev = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= Math.min(i, k); t++) {
      for (let j = t - 1; j < i; j++) {
        const val = dp[j][t - 1] + dist[j][i - 1];
        if (val > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val;
          prev[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  const partitions = [];
  let [i, t] = [n, k];
  while (t > 0) {
    const j = prev[i][t];
    partitions.unshift([j, i - 1]);
    i = j;
    t--;
  }

  return { value: dp[n][k], partitions };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a new DP variant: maximizing the sum of non-additive subarray values (bitwise OR) while enforcing exactly k non-overlapping blocks. It also probes reconstruction logic for end-to-start blocks.

## Key Concepts
- DP over partitioning into k non-overlapping blocks
- Non-additive block value via OR, requiring on-the-fly accumulation
- Backpointers for exact block endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKOrSubarrays(A, k){
  const n=A.length;
  const dp=Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prv=Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0]=0;
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=k;t++){
      let curr=0;
      for(let j=i;j>=0;j--){
        curr |= A[j];
        let left = dp[j][t-1];
        if(left>-Infinity){
          const cand = left + curr;
          if(cand>dp[i+1][t]){ dp[i+1][t]=cand; prv[i+1][t]=j; }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return {value: dp[n][k], endAt: prv};
}
```

